{"title":"2025 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Diagram_(Not_actually_in_competition)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Diagram (Not actually in competition)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Calculus)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Calculus)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Cheese)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Cheese)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Calculus_and_Quadratic,_similar_to_Solution_2)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Calculus and Quadratic, similar to Solution 2)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~1:20)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:20)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(Quick_and_Simple)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(Quick and Simple)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_(Fast_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 (Fast and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/b/e6b71a30cc1c347b34971b1f25595c07e76c1eb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{1}{3}x + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" /> divides the square region defined by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/8/c283793592b9778bcdc15ca397f3164e3155ef5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le x \\le 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/1/56146d0e8464ea4c1910603a8d21274091ef5a2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le y \\le 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> into an upper region and a lower region. The line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/7/e77ba6189a32e5ead2cbb44585ede2285792545c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"10\" /> divides the lower region into two regions of equal area. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/1/2c1568b8a1854d8755b96f2f99851862b1af8534.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{s} - t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"21\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> are positive integers. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/7/0d7d632c02823c5abcda3053a1b38c6b7f311a08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s + t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"39\" height=\"15\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c1694ce726675553e20fbed3649785fd5ebc13ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}~18 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}~19 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}~20 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}~21 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}~22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Diagram_.28Not_actually_in_competition.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Diagram_(Not_actually_in_competition)\">Diagram (Not actually in competition)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Diagram (Not actually in competition)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/5/d752fc0e0aa1e3198c7a98b31ee9cf45cfa9717c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph; unitsize(4cm);   path square = scale(2)*unitsquare; draw(square, linewidth(1.5));   label(&quot;$(0,0)$&quot;, (0,0), SW); label(&quot;$(2,0)$&quot;, (2,0), SE); label(&quot;$(2,2)$&quot;, (2,2), NE); label(&quot;$(0,2)$&quot;, (0,2), NW);     path line1 = (0,1) -- (2, 5/3); draw(line1, black + linewidth(1)); label(&quot;$y=\\frac{x}{3}+1$&quot;, point(line1, 1), E, black);   path line2 = (0,1) -- (2,1); draw(line2, black + linewidth(1)); label(&quot;$y=1$&quot;, point(line2, 1), E, black);  real a = sqrt(17)-3; real x_val = a; path line3 = (x_val, 0) -- (x_val, 2); draw(line3, black + dashed + linewidth(1)); label(&quot;$x=a$&quot;, point(line3, 1), N, black);   dot((x_val, 1), orange);   xaxis(&quot;$x$&quot;, -0.5, 2.5, Arrow); yaxis(&quot;$y$&quot;, -0.5, 2.5, Arrow); [/asy]\" width=\"668\" height=\"668\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We solve this by finding the areas of trapezoids. The line is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/b/e6b71a30cc1c347b34971b1f25595c07e76c1eb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{1}{3}x + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" />.\nTotal Area (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/2/2229aed65193afee61cb7469b5a23d694a7b24cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{\\text{total}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />) of Lower Region:\nThe region from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69271b422e022ea65ff1f288eddfcfa82afd8ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is a trapezoid.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/3/4f399dbb56616de33699128a9b04da6199cd775b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A_{\\text{total}} = \\frac{1}{2}(y(0) + y(2)) \\times (2 - 0) = \\frac{1}{2}\\left(1 + \\frac{5}{3}\\right)(2) = \\frac{8}{3}\\]\" width=\"430\" height=\"43\" />\nHalf Area (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/4/03498888e1831db3bc56067e525705e8e0aeef4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{\\text{half}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"17\" />):\nThe area of the region from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed47ef35959c171399e8f18eed4b517223823c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=a$\" width=\"44\" height=\"8\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/c/6acd98f6a1801667f89a2a53a4ef79eda3a7fafc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}A_{\\text{total}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/9/5898ed8785f6a717a27514450efb7eb0ef207cf2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A_{\\text{half}} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{8}{3} = \\frac{4}{3}\\]\" width=\"144\" height=\"37\" />\nSolve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />:\nThis half-region is also a trapezoid.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/f/6afa7bce2422c0e8006c2410e1ea6bf47e22a195.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A_{\\text{half}} = \\frac{1}{2}(y(0) + y(a)) \\times (a - 0) = \\frac{4}{3}\\]\" width=\"288\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/c/94ce103b8a0eb8316db587fc437d4feae8329839.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}\\left(1 + \\left(\\frac{1}{3}a + 1\\right)\\right)a = \\frac{4}{3}\\]\" width=\"200\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/7/22759025c159624d1c001544541868884113387c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}\\left(2 + \\frac{a}{3}\\right)a = \\frac{4}{3}\\]\" width=\"128\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/b/c1b9dc961302e90808393f5786f350cd01220568.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a + \\frac{a^2}{6} = \\frac{4}{3}\\]\" width=\"88\" height=\"39\" />\nMultiplying by 6 gives the quadratic equation:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/6/6a656069c707f79edbef9eb3b2a6b009fcd61f5a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2 + 6a - 8 = 0\\]\" width=\"121\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/a/81a07c074851ae25714a27e1933a42d582979425.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a = \\frac{-6 \\pm \\sqrt{6^2 - 4(1)(-8)}}{2} = \\frac{-6 \\pm \\sqrt{68}}{2} = \\frac{-6 \\pm 2\\sqrt{17}}{2} = -3 \\pm \\sqrt{17}\\]\" width=\"535\" height=\"41\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> must be positive, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/3/853fdb57d8c409825e27858b9b14765b7b010dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\sqrt{17} - 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"100\" height=\"21\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3bbb89b0366c95382bde59fb0f7bc8374da02be.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s + t = 17 + 3 = 20\\]\" width=\"152\" height=\"14\" />\nThe correct option is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/5/c95f0a8e91ee8bc86714fdc6b956403c477fe69d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>Note: We can find the area of the trapezoid by integrating. We have the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3bdb4942ebd46378fc31f20384db03d25cb0bc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int_{0}^{2} \\frac{1}{3}x + 1 \\ dx = \\frac{1}{6}x^2 + x \\bigg|_{x=0}^{2} = \\frac{8}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"266\" height=\"50\" />. But this sort of destroys the purpose of this simple solution without calculus. With calculus, the solution below would be the most efficient.\n</p><p>~JerryZYang (for note)\n</p><p>~Jonathanmo\n</p><p>~minor edit: xu27yunz\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Calculus.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Calculus)\">Solution 2 (Calculus)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Calculus)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The intersection of the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/b/e6b71a30cc1c347b34971b1f25595c07e76c1eb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{1}{3}x + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" /> and the square is the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/c/eec5fb715c43d949a8733c2520c55048bdb3f302.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, \\frac{5}{3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"46\" height=\"38\" />. The total area of the trapezoid formed by the line and the square is thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/a/46af4de9643408952cf7beefae73d3d90b25eb01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(2)(\\frac{5}{3} + 1) = \\frac{8}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"134\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>The left trapezoidal region's area is equivalent to the area under the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/b/e6b71a30cc1c347b34971b1f25595c07e76c1eb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{1}{3}x + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d348bde3e15456e71734dc2c56fc7425c95927f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/7/e77ba6189a32e5ead2cbb44585ede2285792545c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"10\" />, which can be evaluated using a definite integral. Setting the integral equal to half of the trapezoidal area, we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/d/96d1910bc53cdbbf41350e054035fb41155a4f52.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\int_{0}^{a} \\left(\\frac{x}{3} + 1\\right)\\, dx = \\frac{4}{3}\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/065b1eb85a2cca6311275a54a9402bdbf09cb7bc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{6}a^2 + a = \\frac{4}{3}\\]\" width=\"95\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/6/6a656069c707f79edbef9eb3b2a6b009fcd61f5a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2 + 6a - 8 = 0\\]\" width=\"121\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>We now use the quadratic formula:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/2/c822f815493e18340eb0a0c8eec0a6b999f06fcc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a = \\frac{-6 \\pm \\sqrt{(-6)^2 - 4(1)(-8)}}{2} = \\sqrt{17} - 3\\]\" width=\"325\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/105a4064e6f0f03b09557c6e47bba19f45970cb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17 + 3 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"140\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Milkdrinker\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Cheese.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Cheese)\">Solution 3 (Cheese)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Cheese)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Firstly, we observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/9/549468508d4685d380485596611540cb71017c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 &lt; a &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" />, because the area bounded by the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/1/a8187bc3f8dadf29ecf719d71940683a1ef37659.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{1}{3}x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" /> and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a306093bbd9e0699c65dba033c9483cd379dc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> is less than the area from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a306093bbd9e0699c65dba033c9483cd379dc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/c/c0c67f1e6c098104b1cb8f1cdd6bb16f689ac3e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. We also know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/e/edeb42c14f86b9dbee8c32d84426583b2722b45c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s+t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"39\" height=\"15\" /> must be equal to one of the integers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d111a5e00ee5ea6700bb629994dc629874c505b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> from the answer choices. We can therefore try out possibilities for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> to see whether they satisfy these two conditions, and we indeed find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> must be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/2/db20d536348151663cd638a4e272b015933bbc40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{s}-3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"21\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/e/60eaa7dd8b38324c46b3656fcd3fdcc9f6627319.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s \\in \\left\\{17, 18, 19\\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"121\" height=\"20\" />, because if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/8/a0878b86902f3586c4761c5fdea7c795af9f9312.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s &lt; 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> would have to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to ensure that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/9/549468508d4685d380485596611540cb71017c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 &lt; a &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" />, but then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/9/4991a8005fa25013417c5a51db37a7da397a2a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s+t = s+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" /> would be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />; similarly, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/d/0bd5abbfd8e45574ccb424c6997355ebf2798651.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s &gt; 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />, then we would have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/e/3ce8c8fa179b8f20a5f587d01bbbf31acf8d1e7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s+t \\geq \\sqrt{20}+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"128\" height=\"22\" />, but this is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d111a5e00ee5ea6700bb629994dc629874c505b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />. Moreover, if we assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is in simplest form, this also rules out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/c/65cf02712aad958d1e4372dff5630b29fb376a86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" />. We are accordingly left with either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/9/1f993bad212597e76aa2af7ca1e10796e5bd255b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\sqrt{17}-3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"100\" height=\"21\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/1/4a18366c08062625a3345936768fa2d49a3a3fd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\sqrt{19}-3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"100\" height=\"21\" />, and by simply substituting each of these for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> to see whether it works or not, we determine that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> must indeed be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/a/0dae2f96f1c14bb227561d5bc324269802e9b7c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{17}-3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"21\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/1/de1f7fdcf13751e885c3eb414a290810209d3069.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s+t = 17+3 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"202\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~ToxicWaste\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Calculus_and_Quadratic.2C_similar_to_Solution_2.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Calculus_and_Quadratic,_similar_to_Solution_2)\">Solution 4 (Calculus and Quadratic, similar to Solution 2)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Calculus and Quadratic, similar to Solution 2)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We consider the lower region defined by the set of points \\( (x, y) \\) inside the square with \\( 0 \\le x \\le 2 \\), \\( 0 \\le y \\le 2 \\) and lying below the line \\( y = \\frac{1}{3}x + 1 \\). Instead of directly integrating, we parametrize this line in an unnecessarily complicated form: write \\( x = 3(t - 1) \\), so \\( y = t \\). This parametrization makes no geometric sense for area, so we abandon it immediately and return to Cartesian coordinates.\n</p><p>The area of the lower region is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/73703c288a01a466101e4f1afc05f3f37920e87d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A_{\\text{lower}} = \\int_0^2 \\left(\\frac{1}{3}x + 1\\right) dx.\\]\" width=\"204\" height=\"45\" />\nRather than compute this, we expand the integrand into a Taylor polynomial about \\( x = 1 \\) even though it is already linear. The Taylor expansion is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/2/53235d03333a1f4128a22eba0d094c056ef2db14.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{3}x + 1 = \\left(\\frac{1}{3}(1) + 1\\right) + \\frac{1}{3}(x - 1) = \\frac{4}{3} + \\frac{1}{3}(x - 1).\\]\" width=\"394\" height=\"43\" />\nIntegrating this form:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/5/de5018074fa3c409d826e5d7c7728ea4039ef184.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A_{\\text{lower}} = \\int_0^2 \\left(\\frac{4}{3} + \\frac{1}{3}(x - 1)\\right) dx.\\]\" width=\"254\" height=\"45\" />\nCompute each part separately even though it's pointless:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/c/f1c5d78872c2ebae8a86e7f5c641a344dff29322.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\int_0^2 \\frac{4}{3} \\, dx = \\frac{8}{3}, \\quad \\int_0^2 \\frac{1}{3}(x - 1) \\, dx = \\frac{1}{3}\\left[\\frac{1}{2}x^2 - x\\right]_0^2 = \\frac{1}{3}(2 - 2) = 0.\\]\" width=\"504\" height=\"47\" />\nThus \\( A_{\\text{lower}} = \\frac{8}{3} \\), matching the normal computation.\n</p><p>Half of this is \\(\\frac{4}{3}\\). So the vertical line \\( x = a \\) must satisfy\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/a/fbac60c743f2c0bdbe480fc620a906dd9dfadafe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\int_0^a \\left(\\frac{1}{3}x + 1\\right) dx = \\frac{4}{3}.\\]\" width=\"173\" height=\"43\" />\nNow we sabotage this simple integral by performing a substitution. Let \\( u = \\frac{1}{3}x + 1 \\), so \\( x = 3(u - 1) \\) and \\( dx = 3 \\, du \\). When \\( x = 0 \\), \\( u = 1 \\). When \\( x = a \\), \\( u = \\frac{1}{3}a + 1 \\). The integral becomes\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/f/6cfb82d716a98baae505d23eae0cb6914ee54b2e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\int_{u=1}^{u=\\frac{1}{3}a + 1} u \\cdot 3 \\, du = 3 \\int_1^{\\frac{1}{3}a + 1} u \\, du.\\]\" width=\"257\" height=\"46\" />\nEvaluate this:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/9/6091e29f273c5d632d65cc376113a969a2da5ec0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3\\left[\\frac{1}{2}u^2\\right]_1^{\\frac{1}{3}a + 1} = \\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\left(\\frac{1}{3}a + 1\\right)^2 - 1\\right).\\]\" width=\"290\" height=\"53\" />\nWe set this equal to \\(\\frac{4}{3}\\):\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/4/5f471b0d1d454d939d2d5494595350143f42fc2a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\left(\\frac{1}{3}a + 1\\right)^2 - 1\\right) = \\frac{4}{3}.\\]\" width=\"202\" height=\"53\" />\nMultiply both sides by 2:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/c/a6c1768b2bc69ee1a4a091199f49dcb3b8d48303.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3\\left(\\left(\\frac{1}{3}a + 1\\right)^2 - 1\\right) = \\frac{8}{3}.\\]\" width=\"199\" height=\"53\" />\nMultiply both sides by 3:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/3/d73a96a9d397704df5715caa494af15c56862504.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9\\left(\\left(\\frac{1}{3}a + 1\\right)^2 - 1\\right) = 8.\\]\" width=\"195\" height=\"53\" />\nNow expand:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f3999417a6628641b454b609f78fec2a41bfb7a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\frac{1}{3}a + 1\\right)^2 = \\frac{1}{9}a^2 + \\frac{2}{3}a + 1.\\]\" width=\"218\" height=\"46\" />\nSubstitute:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/0/8f05e8866424268fe909b9645399432dc3d484b9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9\\left(\\frac{1}{9}a^2 + \\frac{2}{3}a + 1 - 1\\right) = 8.\\]\" width=\"212\" height=\"43\" />\nCancel the ones:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/f/02f162b07457629cc7ecbf08c71457befcad82a5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9\\left(\\frac{1}{9}a^2 + \\frac{2}{3}a\\right) = 8.\\]\" width=\"149\" height=\"43\" />\nDistribute the 9:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/3/d136afe9f29c150cec21edfa3f4398457e4021c7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2 + 6a = 8.\\]\" width=\"94\" height=\"17\" />\nWe arrive—after that absurd detour—at the same quadratic as before.\n</p><p>Solve the quadratic using a deliberately bloated method. Complete the square:\n</p><p>Start with:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50d3e53df22cb31e5aa72907a493e900551b4290.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2 + 6a - 8 = 0.\\]\" width=\"125\" height=\"17\" />\nMove the constant:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/3/d136afe9f29c150cec21edfa3f4398457e4021c7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2 + 6a = 8.\\]\" width=\"94\" height=\"17\" />\nAdd 9 to both sides because \\((6/2)^2 = 9\\):\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/0/e20673b6ff174019111316336846d2416a1e7165.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2 + 6a + 9 = 17.\\]\" width=\"134\" height=\"17\" />\nLeft-hand side is \\((a + 3)^2\\):\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/7/ff72548304849292a9bf7f9929041a5e30e71229.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a + 3)^2 = 17.\\]\" width=\"106\" height=\"20\" />\nTake square roots:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/d/86d686dc186a8af24621a35fd03bcf097d273246.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a + 3 = \\pm \\sqrt{17}.\\]\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/a/56a31dc55a264882d53a10d4faa16e974c025c80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\in [0,2]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"20\" />, take the positive root:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/0/3d0ea0e608d6dfd429a16a0e60ac2288d5d9447d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a = \\sqrt{17} - 3.\\]\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" />\nThis matches the form \\( \\sqrt{s} - t \\) with \\( s = 17, t = 3 \\).\nThus\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/8/b08b0e7d38f2753c101b730d0669f929699acdc0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s + t = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 20}.\\]\" width=\"129\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~notvalid\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/b/e6b71a30cc1c347b34971b1f25595c07e76c1eb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{1}{3}x + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" /> intersects the square at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be11a56a55425d6c6b69f70f5fa98eab95e8ad18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/a/4fa6759259516b246100234ce13ffa499a2c2398.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,\\frac{5}{3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"46\" height=\"38\" />. Consider the region bounded by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/b/17b844be6efb85bbcb3fecf44f06371a3a68ae4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0), (0,1), (2,\\frac{5}{3}), (2,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"192\" height=\"38\" />. By Shoelace Formula that is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39c759c3d65f9971373f64fd883f534f4456d416.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2} |(0 \\cdot 1 + 0 \\cdot \\frac{5}{3} + 2 \\cdot 0 + 2 \\cdot 0) - (0 \\cdot 0 + 1 \\cdot 2 + \\frac{10}{3} + 0 \\cdot 0)| = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{16}{3} = \\frac{8}{3}\\]\" width=\"536\" height=\"38\" />.\nHence the area of the region is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/f/24f4606bd5646f403a4676964fe7fea017583c28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />. Now, add in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7575486863a33508063b4fd5977609074f6c2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x =a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"10\" />, and a new region bounded by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/a/c9a1f1f90912b33bb102297fd27b841acb7ab599.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0), (0,1), (a, \\frac{a}{3} + 1), (a,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"225\" height=\"34\" /> exists that is half this area. By Shoelace Formula,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/a/eeaa18a353c37affd316e9e5e36913953b847d6a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}|(0 \\cdot 1 + 0 \\cdot \\frac{a}{3}+1 + a \\cdot 0 + a \\cdot 0) - (0 \\cdot 0 + 1 \\cdot a + (\\frac{a^2}{3}+a)+0 \\cdot 0)| = \\frac{1}{2}|2a+\\frac{a^2}{3}| = a + \\frac{a^2}{6}\\]\" width=\"568\" height=\"39\" />.\nSo one can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/3/a63864d4bcb18b609fc6666db6e6d7e3db626d45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + \\frac{a^2}{6} = \\frac{4}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"92\" height=\"41\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/d/1fd83416e410389646391ca34a0a6341fc6cedc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a + \\frac{a^2}{2} = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"41\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/8/ad84fa72530b79c5c39461d46f190193ec1aafda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6a + a^2 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" />. In that case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/6/2362b80de6575245e0ffcaa05c1ed7ce6df5c1f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + 6a - 8 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/b/6ab6dc2e1444a2de1f4c9d9c9b6391b27b4040ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{-6 \\pm \\sqrt{68}}{2} = -3 \\pm \\sqrt{17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"221\" height=\"43\" />. Notice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> lies in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/0/680a8d46bc22febe67556eecd2b33b35ace846eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(+,+)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" /> quadrant I, hence negate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/0/6b05fa6517db4c2d3c0280e94f4707a6e6ac29fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3-\\sqrt{17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"81\" height=\"21\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/f/8cff1789c782d9d36ebcc020f9890ca47303c44d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\sqrt{17} - 3 \\implies \\boxed{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"179\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_.28Logical.2C_Good_Editing.2C_.7E1:20.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~1:20)\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:20)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:20)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/kuCphxoN2do\">https://www.youtube.com/shorts/kuCphxoN2do</a>\n</p><p>~Ebai\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/vayQuXXbr28\">https://youtu.be/vayQuXXbr28</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.28Quick_and_Simple.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(Quick_and_Simple)\">Video Solution(Quick and Simple)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution(Quick and Simple)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0clKakfcraY\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0clKakfcraY</a>\n~Sigma_Bob\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dLSWVrrKsgs\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dLSWVrrKsgs</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_2_.28Fast_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_(Fast_and_Easy)\">Video Solution 2 (Fast and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 (Fast and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=